1047
00:41:07,273 --> 00:41:09,602
- But you have to make those moves. - Really?

1048
00:41:09,603 --> 00:41:10,972
You have to make yourself known.

1049
00:41:10,973 --> 00:41:13,573
I'm not asking you right now for a duet,

1050
00:41:13,873 --> 00:41:17,882
but there are some lyrics that I wrote...

1051
00:41:17,883 --> 00:41:19,112
while imagining doing a duet with you.

1052
00:41:19,113 --> 00:41:20,143
Right. Let's see them.

1053
00:41:20,283 --> 00:41:21,883
- Bring them over. - That's great.

1054
00:41:23,553 --> 00:41:25,222
I've been writing a lot of lyrics these days.

1055
00:41:25,223 --> 00:41:27,053
- Is that so? - I've been writing a lot.

1056
00:41:27,393 --> 00:41:29,093
- I came up with them briefly. - Right.

1057
00:41:29,893 --> 00:41:31,722
- Well... - This never happened.

1058
00:41:31,723 --> 00:41:33,633
It's important to be different.

1059
00:41:33,963 --> 00:41:37,963
I don't think I remember seeing a men's duet.

1060
00:41:38,203 --> 00:41:40,902
May I read the lyrics to you?

1061
00:41:40,903 --> 00:41:42,103
Sure.

1062
00:41:42,933 --> 00:41:44,402
I'm quite lacking now,

1063
00:41:44,403 --> 00:41:46,342
but I wrote those lyrics while dreaming of that day.

1064
00:41:46,343 --> 00:41:47,943
That must be really embarrassing.

1065
00:41:50,343 --> 00:41:51,383
Go on.

1066
00:41:53,783 --> 00:41:54,853
First of all,

1067
00:41:55,753 --> 00:41:59,782
the title is "Eighty-One, Thirty-One."

1068
00:41:59,783 --> 00:42:01,952
- It was made with him in mind. - Right.

1069
00:42:01,953 --> 00:42:03,793
- The first verse is your part. - Right.

1070
00:42:04,323 --> 00:42:06,293
(Ready to listen)

1071
00:42:07,963 --> 00:42:10,163
"I'm no longer ambitious now."

1072
00:42:10,763 --> 00:42:12,403
"I've done all I can."

1073
00:42:13,063 --> 00:42:16,172
"Passionate love, loyal friendship,"

1074
00:42:16,173 --> 00:42:17,403
"and wandering about immaturely."

1075
00:42:17,843 --> 00:42:20,512
"I want to lie on that vast beach."

1076
00:42:20,513 --> 00:42:21,613
(I want to lie on that vast beach)

1077
00:42:22,513 --> 00:42:23,813
- The second verse. - Right.

1078
00:42:24,483 --> 00:42:26,343
"I'm still full of ambition."

1079
00:42:26,913 --> 00:42:28,613
"I like dancing and having fun."

1080
00:42:28,783 --> 00:42:30,113
"I love my friends."

1081
00:42:30,823 --> 00:42:34,023
"I want to run around that vast beach."

1082
00:42:34,993 --> 00:42:37,992
"Gosh, I will run like crazy."

1083
00:42:37,993 --> 00:42:42,163
(Gosh, I will run like crazy.)

1084
00:42:42,233 --> 00:42:45,133
"Gosh, I will run like crazy."

1085
00:42:46,133 --> 00:42:47,403
(Embarrassed)

1086
00:42:47,633 --> 00:42:49,503
(How were my lyrics?)

1087
00:42:50,803 --> 00:42:52,472
He doesn't look so happy.

1088
00:42:52,473 --> 00:42:53,813
His face stiffened.

1089
00:42:54,213 --> 00:42:55,572
Your part might be what he has in his heart.

1090
00:42:55,573 --> 00:42:57,312
(I want to run around that vast beach.)

1091
00:42:57,313 --> 00:42:58,982
He's still young in heart!

1092
00:42:58,983 --> 00:43:01,183
"You should stop now and get some rest."

1093
00:43:01,253 --> 00:43:03,113
"Why must I be lying around on the beach?"

1094
00:43:03,353 --> 00:43:04,952
- Why make him like that? - "I still want to be in love."

1095
00:43:04,953 --> 00:43:06,623
- Gosh. - "I'm still young in heart."

1096
00:43:06,823 --> 00:43:10,692
That wasn't my intention. I wanted to write lyrics...

1097
00:43:10,693 --> 00:43:12,292
about a senior in life.

1098
00:43:12,293 --> 00:43:13,792
What makes him more like a senior...

1099
00:43:13,793 --> 00:43:15,992
is for the one that is 81...

1100
00:43:15,993 --> 00:43:18,062
to sing that he still is ambitious at that age.

1101
00:43:18,063 --> 00:43:20,302
- That's a lot more impressive. - It's better to switch it around.

1102
00:43:20,303 --> 00:43:22,903
- Right. That's a great idea. - That's great.

1103
00:43:23,503 --> 00:43:24,772
(Feeling proud)

1104
00:43:24,773 --> 00:43:26,442
Make sure to make a lot of changes to the lyrics.

1105
00:43:26,443 --> 00:43:27,712
Right. I will have to.

1106
00:43:27,713 --> 00:43:29,273
(What will Jin think?)

1107
00:43:29,443 --> 00:43:30,912
- That's great. - Right.

1108
00:43:30,913 --> 00:43:33,542
It feels passionate and realistic.

1109
00:43:33,543 --> 00:43:35,013
Were you always talented in writing?

1110
00:43:35,383 --> 00:43:37,952
- Were you into writing in school? - Well, no.

1111
00:43:37,953 --> 00:43:39,522
I was never into writing.

1112
00:43:39,523 --> 00:43:40,892
You must've read a lot of books.

1113
00:43:40,893 --> 00:43:42,853
- I've only read one book. - Right.

1114
00:43:43,393 --> 00:43:44,663
"So that explains."

1115
00:43:44,723 --> 00:43:46,822
"No wonder."

1116
00:43:46,823 --> 00:43:48,262
"Right. No wonder."

1117
00:43:48,263 --> 00:43:50,062
- "I see. Read some books." - "I see now."

1118
00:43:50,063 --> 00:43:51,833
"That explains everything."

1119
00:43:52,103 --> 00:43:54,302
I'm the worst when it comes to writing.

1120
00:43:54,303 --> 00:43:56,232
- Why would you say that? - No. I'm serious.

1121
00:43:56,233 --> 00:43:57,972
I haven't read a lot of books.

1122
00:43:57,973 --> 00:44:00,043
- I've only read one. - Right.

1123
00:44:00,273 --> 00:44:02,672
You've read one book, at least. I haven't read a single book.

1124
00:44:02,673 --> 00:44:04,443
You're better than me.

1125
00:44:05,213 --> 00:44:07,683
He didn't say anything about doing a duet though.

1126
00:44:09,613 --> 00:44:11,623
To me, Nam Jin...

1127
00:44:12,053 --> 00:44:15,053
feels like a reliable tree that has been around for a while.

1128
00:44:15,423 --> 00:44:18,692
Just like he is right now,

1129
00:44:18,693 --> 00:44:20,833
no matter how many years pass by,

1130
00:44:21,193 --> 00:44:23,863
I wish for him to be happy...

1131
00:44:23,963 --> 00:44:26,133
and healthy for a long time.

1132
00:44:26,363 --> 00:44:28,402
I just wish him to be healthy.

1133
00:44:28,403 --> 00:44:29,473
(A strong pillar that kept him dreaming)

1134
00:44:29,933 --> 00:44:33,203
A brother forever, and our Nam Jin forever.

1135
00:44:33,303 --> 00:44:36,013
That is what my heart wishes him to be.

1136
00:44:38,913 --> 00:44:42,082
(My Idol and Strong Pillar Forever)

1137
00:44:42,083 --> 00:44:43,113
(I Live Alone)

1138
00:44:43,753 --> 00:44:46,583
(Bok Has Come)

1139
00:44:47,393 --> 00:44:48,423
(Groaning)

1140
00:44:49,553 --> 00:44:51,193
There's so much extra space on the bed.

1141
00:44:51,523 --> 00:44:52,663
Right.

1142
00:44:54,033 --> 00:44:55,533
Gosh, my shoulder hurts.

1143
00:44:56,793 --> 00:44:59,863
My shoulder hurts a lot as I have to use a lot of my forearm.

1144
00:45:00,573 --> 00:45:01,773
You're using your forearm these days?

1145
00:45:03,703 --> 00:45:06,103
(What time is it?)

1146
00:45:07,243 --> 00:45:09,573
(Getting up)

1147
00:45:10,983 --> 00:45:14,383
(She gets up right away without any hesitation.)

1148
00:45:14,513 --> 00:45:15,852
I got up early in the morning.

1149
00:45:15,853 --> 00:45:17,623
I usually never wake up at that time.

1150
00:45:19,583 --> 00:45:22,653
(She moves quickly in the morning on her day off.)

1151
00:45:25,023 --> 00:45:26,263
Bokdol!

1152
00:45:27,363 --> 00:45:28,533
Bokdol!

1153
00:45:28,993 --> 00:45:30,193
Did you sleep well?

1154
00:45:33,333 --> 00:45:35,433
(There's a dog in Na Rae's house?)

1155
00:45:37,503 --> 00:45:40,203
I am Park Na Rae, who doesn't live alone anymore.

1156
00:45:40,813 --> 00:45:43,643
- This is Bokdol. - Gosh!

1157
00:45:44,043 --> 00:45:46,513
It's a male dog that is five.

1158
00:45:46,713 --> 00:45:49,413
He's my new pet friend.

1159
00:45:49,553 --> 00:45:51,083
- Gosh! - He's smiling!

1160
00:45:51,153 --> 00:45:52,282
Bokdol loves smiling.

1161
00:45:52,283 --> 00:45:53,423
- He's adorable. - The dog has a smiley face.

1162
00:45:54,823 --> 00:45:58,263
(During dinner at Na Rae's grandparents' house...)

1163
00:45:59,423 --> 00:46:02,533
(when the three were there to clear up the place)

1164
00:46:03,163 --> 00:46:06,063
(There's a Jindo dog that my grandfather raised.)

1165
00:46:06,163 --> 00:46:07,633
(His name is Bokdol.)

1166
00:46:08,873 --> 00:46:12,703
(The dog was sent to the hospital for a health check.)

1167
00:46:13,443 --> 00:46:17,313
(After my grandfather passed away,)

1168
00:46:17,483 --> 00:46:19,483
(I kept thinking about Bokdol.)

1169
00:46:20,113 --> 00:46:22,253
(Don't worry and raise him. I'll help you.)

1170
00:46:22,713 --> 00:46:26,283
(I think Bokdol will bring a lot of good things to you.)

1171
00:46:27,053 --> 00:46:28,622
The two of them strongly recommended...

1172
00:46:28,623 --> 00:46:30,692
that I should raise Bokdol.

1173
00:46:30,693 --> 00:46:33,063
That was why I made that big decision.

1174
00:46:33,423 --> 00:46:34,733
"I'll take him home tomorrow."

1175
00:46:35,263 --> 00:46:36,862
It has been around two months and a half...

1176
00:46:36,863 --> 00:46:38,503
since I've lived with Bokdol.

1177
00:46:39,833 --> 00:46:42,003
- He's so cute! - He looks handsome.

1178
00:46:42,133 --> 00:46:43,603
- It's a brindle. - Right.

1179
00:46:43,833 --> 00:46:46,642
I'm a total rookie when it comes to raising dogs.

1180
00:46:46,643 --> 00:46:49,412
Him and I are both...

1181
00:46:49,413 --> 00:46:50,982
are trying our best to adjust to each other.

1182
00:46:50,983 --> 00:46:53,212
- I need your help as my seniors. - Right.

1183
00:46:53,213 --> 00:46:55,682
I've asked everyone around me including Ki Bum.

1184
00:46:55,683 --> 00:46:56,882
- Please help me. - Of course.

1185
00:46:56,883 --> 00:46:58,252
- There's Lee Jung as well. - I will definitely help.

1186
00:46:58,253 --> 00:47:00,482
Everyone except for President Jun...

1187
00:47:00,483 --> 00:47:02,052
has a pet cat...

1188
00:47:02,053 --> 00:47:04,393
- or a pet dog. - Right.

1189
00:47:05,163 --> 00:47:06,923
(Butlers and cat experts)

1190
00:47:07,023 --> 00:47:08,692
I'm also a dog expert.

1191
00:47:08,693 --> 00:47:10,832
- Really? - But I had to send mine away.

1192
00:47:10,833 --> 00:47:12,232
(Pookie)

1193
00:47:12,233 --> 00:47:13,762
Right. You've lived with your dog for a long time.

1194
00:47:13,763 --> 00:47:15,102
I've lived with my dog for a long time.

1195
00:47:15,103 --> 00:47:16,503
(Feeling grateful)

1196
00:47:17,203 --> 00:47:18,743
As for Bokdol,

1197
00:47:18,973 --> 00:47:22,142
he's quite small for a Jindo dog.

1198
00:47:22,143 --> 00:47:25,742
He's like the small giant of Jindo dogs like Park Na Rae.

1199
00:47:25,743 --> 00:47:26,743
This is who Park Bokdol is.

1200
00:47:27,583 --> 00:47:29,782
- Dogs take after their owners. - He's a small giant.

1201
00:47:29,783 --> 00:47:31,883
- You two were destined to meet. - He's a bit small.

1202
00:47:31,983 --> 00:47:34,492
- You love the leopard print. - I absolutely do.

1203
00:47:34,493 --> 00:47:35,553
What a match.

1204
00:47:35,793 --> 00:47:37,722
- That's why I love him even more. - He's just like his owner.

1205
00:47:37,723 --> 00:47:38,993
(They are just like each other with their fancy looks.)

1206
00:47:39,163 --> 00:47:40,393
He loves people...

1207
00:47:40,893 --> 00:47:42,293
and has great memory.

1208
00:47:43,093 --> 00:47:45,403
He remembers every single person just after seeing them once.

1209
00:47:46,503 --> 00:47:47,503
He's adorable.

1210
00:47:47,504 --> 00:47:48,533
(Eyes full of love)

1211
00:47:48,973 --> 00:47:51,073
(For this cute and small giant,)

1212
00:47:51,943 --> 00:47:52,972
(Na Rae made a place for him on the 1st floor.)

1213
00:47:52,973 --> 00:47:55,442
I can't believe I'm seeing this at Na Rae's house.

1214
00:47:55,443 --> 00:47:56,642
Right.

1215
00:47:56,643 --> 00:47:59,383
Who would've expected to see that at my house?

1216
00:48:00,343 --> 00:48:03,553
(There are dog items all around the house.)

1217
00:48:04,353 --> 00:48:06,182
This is a great place for Bokdol.

1218
00:48:06,183 --> 00:48:07,493
(Na Rae's house has changed for Bokdol.)

1219
00:48:07,953 --> 00:48:08,992
Bokdol!

1220
00:48:08,993 --> 00:48:11,223
(Laughing)

1221
00:48:12,063 --> 00:48:14,692
You're so excited.

1222
00:48:14,693 --> 00:48:15,793
(Excited)

1223
00:48:16,193 --> 00:48:17,932
Gosh, what is going on?

1224
00:48:17,933 --> 00:48:19,262
(She opens the fence while greeting him in the morning.)

1225
00:48:19,263 --> 00:48:22,173
Come out, Bokdol.

1226
00:48:22,673 --> 00:48:24,343
(Rushing out)

1227
00:48:25,273 --> 00:48:27,173
- How exciting! - Gosh.

1228
00:48:27,373 --> 00:48:28,913
He's so cute!

1229
00:48:29,213 --> 00:48:30,273
Come here.

1230
00:48:32,813 --> 00:48:34,153
You're so adorable.

1231
00:48:36,353 --> 00:48:37,822
(She gives him a morning pat with all of her care.)

1232
00:48:37,823 --> 00:48:39,252
Isn't this really nice?

1233
00:48:39,253 --> 00:48:41,692
You have a presence to look for...

1234
00:48:41,693 --> 00:48:42,952
- right after waking up. - Right.

1235
00:48:42,953 --> 00:48:44,622
- You're greeted in the morning. - Right.

1236
00:48:44,623 --> 00:48:46,362
I've been with them every single day for 13 years,

1237
00:48:46,363 --> 00:48:48,362
but they greet me every single morning.

1238
00:48:48,363 --> 00:48:49,762
Right.

1239
00:48:49,763 --> 00:48:52,503
They wag their tails like crazy.

1240
00:48:52,903 --> 00:48:54,732
It feels really weird to me.

1241
00:48:54,733 --> 00:48:56,232
- Right? - It's because...

1242
00:48:56,233 --> 00:48:58,502
Bokdol and I...

1243
00:48:58,503 --> 00:49:01,012
started living together right after our blind date.

1244
00:49:01,013 --> 00:49:02,812
- Right. - It must feel like a dating show.

1245
00:49:02,813 --> 00:49:04,983
It does feel like a dating show.

1246
00:49:05,283 --> 00:49:06,842
The house feels like one from a dating show as well.

1247
00:49:06,843 --> 00:49:07,953
Totally.

1248
00:49:09,583 --> 00:49:11,823
(We've started living together right from the start.)

1249
00:49:12,583 --> 00:49:14,723
(Park Na Rae, 40, comedienne)

1250
00:49:15,553 --> 00:49:18,093
(Bokdol, 5, home protector)

1251
00:49:18,563 --> 00:49:22,033
We're slowly adjusting to each other at our own pace.

1252
00:49:23,193 --> 00:49:24,762
I won't try to rush things.

1253
00:49:24,763 --> 00:49:25,763
Right.

1254
00:49:27,673 --> 00:49:29,603
Bokdol, go out and poop.

1255
00:49:30,943 --> 00:49:32,073
Go out and poop.

1256
00:49:32,203 --> 00:49:34,112
Does he only poop outside?

1257
00:49:34,113 --> 00:49:36,373
He pees on the dog pad...

1258
00:49:36,773 --> 00:49:37,912
and poops outside.

1259
00:49:37,913 --> 00:49:40,043
- I see. He's a smart dog. - I see.

1260
00:49:42,113 --> 00:49:43,983
What is all this? What a mess.

1261
00:49:44,853 --> 00:49:45,983
A total mess.

1262
00:49:46,783 --> 00:49:49,252
- Gosh! - It's a total mess.

1263
00:49:49,253 --> 00:49:51,062
- It's a flood. - I got so surprised.

1264
00:49:51,063 --> 00:49:52,323
- Right. - Right.

1265
00:49:53,723 --> 00:49:57,663
(She gets the cleaning tools first.)

1266
00:49:58,503 --> 00:49:59,503
Gosh.

1267
00:49:59,663 --> 00:50:02,833
(She soaks it up with the dog pad first.)

1268
00:50:04,143 --> 00:50:05,702
When you raise a dog,

1269
00:50:05,703 --> 00:50:07,642
you have to start the day by cleaning that up.

1270
00:50:07,643 --> 00:50:09,343
The dog pad has to be cleaned up.

1271
00:50:09,713 --> 00:50:11,842
Na Rae is in our world now.

1272
00:50:11,843 --> 00:50:13,113
(A familiar sight)

1273
00:50:14,613 --> 00:50:18,423
(She wipes the floor cleanly.)

1274
00:50:20,153 --> 00:50:22,393
(There we go.)

1275
00:50:23,193 --> 00:50:24,263
Done.

1276
00:50:25,093 --> 00:50:27,063
The dog pad is huge.

1277
00:50:27,293 --> 00:50:28,662
It's big enough for a person to use.

1278
00:50:28,663 --> 00:50:29,693
(Feeling proud)

1279
00:50:30,933 --> 00:50:33,303
(She heads outside after placing the large dog pad.)

1280
00:50:34,233 --> 00:50:35,973
Where did you poop, Bokdol?

1281
00:50:37,443 --> 00:50:39,473
(It's over there.)

1282
00:50:39,843 --> 00:50:41,572
Where? Did you poop there?

1283
00:50:41,573 --> 00:50:42,843
(He leads the way after smartly understanding her.)

1284
00:50:43,543 --> 00:50:44,712
(Disgusted)

1285
00:50:44,713 --> 00:50:46,213
- Bokdol! - What's wrong?

1286
00:50:46,383 --> 00:50:48,853
- My goodness. - Gosh.

1287
00:50:49,413 --> 00:50:52,423
Good job!

1288
00:50:52,753 --> 00:50:54,923
(Good job, my Bokdol.)

1289
00:50:55,123 --> 00:50:56,553
Good job.

1290
00:50:57,153 --> 00:50:58,392
(Unlike Bokdol who is excited after getting complimented...)

1291
00:50:58,393 --> 00:51:00,562
- He's excited. - He's totally excited.

1292
00:51:00,563 --> 00:51:01,663
Good job.

1293
00:51:02,293 --> 00:51:04,803
(Closing her eyes)

1294
00:51:05,803 --> 00:51:07,002
Gosh, it's warm.

1295
00:51:07,003 --> 00:51:08,802
It's warm when you touch it at that moment.

1296
00:51:08,803 --> 00:51:10,333
(That warmth is hard to get used to even after many times.)

1297
00:51:10,733 --> 00:51:14,173
It's massive in size with big dogs.

1298
00:51:15,413 --> 00:51:18,613
Doing things a regular basis and following a routine?

1299
00:51:19,243 --> 00:51:20,883
I'm someone who never does that.

1300
00:51:21,213 --> 00:51:23,653
But there was a change after meeting him.

1301
00:51:24,053 --> 00:51:25,753
Just for Bokdol,

1302
00:51:26,553 --> 00:51:28,422
there are things I have to do...

1303
00:51:28,423 --> 00:51:29,923
- in the morning. - Right.

1304
00:51:30,093 --> 00:51:31,793
It has become a routine.

1305
00:51:32,323 --> 00:51:33,863
Those are things you must do.

1306
00:51:34,493 --> 00:51:35,992
I get up early now.

1307
00:51:35,993 --> 00:51:37,163
(Thank you, Na Rae.)

1308
00:51:38,863 --> 00:51:41,133
(While Bokdol is running around,)

1309
00:51:44,173 --> 00:51:46,843
(she gets out dried pollack.)

1310
00:51:47,873 --> 00:51:50,343
As he's a dog from Mokpo,

1311
00:51:50,913 --> 00:51:52,183
he likes fish more than meat.

1312
00:51:54,713 --> 00:51:56,052
- Gosh. - Gosh.

1313
00:51:56,053 --> 00:51:58,152
She's preparing a meal for the dog before her own meal.

1314
00:51:58,153 --> 00:51:59,523
Gosh!

1315
00:52:00,623 --> 00:52:02,623
(She quickly washes even the sweet potato.)

1316
00:52:05,023 --> 00:52:08,693
(Bokdol's breakfast is prepared in a hurry.)

1317
00:52:10,533 --> 00:52:12,963
(She comes out to the living room while the sweet potato cooks.)

1318
00:52:13,303 --> 00:52:14,373
Bokdol?

1319
00:52:15,203 --> 00:52:16,233
Bokdol.

1320
00:52:18,703 --> 00:52:20,442
He knows his name.

1321
00:52:20,443 --> 00:52:21,913
He comes when I call his name around five times.

1322
00:52:22,343 --> 00:52:23,473
Should we eat now?

1323
00:52:24,283 --> 00:52:25,743
Should we eat? Let's eat.

1324
00:52:26,413 --> 00:52:28,153
This is your favorite, dried pollack.

1325
00:52:28,683 --> 00:52:29,883
Do you want some dried pollack?

1326
00:52:31,253 --> 00:52:32,483
- Wait here. - He's excited.

1327
00:52:33,183 --> 00:52:34,252
Don't come up.

1328
00:52:34,253 --> 00:52:36,492
- So he's not allowed to go up. - Really?

1329
00:52:36,493 --> 00:52:38,593
- This is our rule. - You're doing great.

1330
00:52:39,063 --> 00:52:40,292
I have a lot of guests that come over...

1331
00:52:40,293 --> 00:52:41,632
and my house has...

1332
00:52:41,633 --> 00:52:42,962
- so many different things. - Right.

1333
00:52:42,963 --> 00:52:44,862
There's food and dangerous objects.

1334
00:52:44,863 --> 00:52:46,403
That is why I limited his space to the first floor.

1335
00:52:46,603 --> 00:52:48,133
That makes sense.

1336
00:52:48,573 --> 00:52:51,173
(Only Na Rae goes up as they keep their own rule.)

1337
00:52:51,743 --> 00:52:54,173
(He follows Na Rae.)

1338
00:52:55,043 --> 00:52:57,113
(He stops right in front of the staircase.)

1339
00:52:58,583 --> 00:53:00,612
I made it certain. That is how we can live together!

1340
00:53:00,613 --> 00:53:02,683
I said that, but...

1341
00:53:04,783 --> 00:53:06,283
He must be really hungry.

1342
00:53:08,323 --> 00:53:10,453
No, Bokdol!

1343
00:53:10,793 --> 00:53:13,963
We promised each other that you won't come up, Bokdol.

1344
00:53:14,363 --> 00:53:15,793
You remember our rule, don't you?

1345
00:53:15,893 --> 00:53:17,063
You're a bad dog if you come up.

1346
00:53:18,133 --> 00:53:19,133
I'm sorry.

1347
00:53:19,134 --> 00:53:20,262
(I'm sorry for sending you away.)

1348
00:53:20,263 --> 00:53:22,002
- Bokdol. - He listens well though.

1349
00:53:22,003 --> 00:53:23,173
He listens well.

1350
00:53:23,873 --> 00:53:25,243
You're a bad dog if you come up.

1351
00:53:30,243 --> 00:53:31,882
Bokdol is a bad dog.

1352
00:53:31,883 --> 00:53:33,613
He's a bad boy.

1353
00:53:34,183 --> 00:53:35,713
You're a bad dog if you come up.

1354
00:53:36,813 --> 00:53:37,953
He still goes back down.

1355
00:53:38,683 --> 00:53:41,093
(Whining)

1356
00:53:42,023 --> 00:53:44,093
You're a bad dog if you come up. Come here.

1357
00:53:45,893 --> 00:53:46,922
You look excited.

1358
00:53:46,923 --> 00:53:48,093
(Slowly moving over)

1359
00:53:48,593 --> 00:53:50,633
(Where is he going?)

1360
00:53:50,793 --> 00:53:51,903
You look excited.

1361
00:53:52,663 --> 00:53:54,572
- He's so curious. - He must want to go up.

1362
00:53:54,573 --> 00:53:56,003
Bokdol!

1363
00:53:58,843 --> 00:54:00,272
(He keeps going up the stairs.)

1364
00:54:00,273 --> 00:54:03,542
It's hard to tell if he's going to listen or not.

1365
00:54:03,543 --> 00:54:05,013
It's hard to communicate as a dog and an owner.

1366
00:54:06,213 --> 00:54:07,443
Stay inside for just a while.

1367
00:54:08,253 --> 00:54:09,683
The ultimate treat.

1368
00:54:10,853 --> 00:54:12,783
You will have to follow this.

1369
00:54:15,123 --> 00:54:17,793
I'll feed you if you stay inside for just a while.

1370
00:54:18,493 --> 00:54:19,823
I should go in first.

1371
00:54:20,793 --> 00:54:21,833
Come here.

1372
00:54:23,133 --> 00:54:24,292
Stay here for just a while.

1373
00:54:24,293 --> 00:54:25,863
(She manages to bring him in with the treat.)

1374
00:54:26,203 --> 00:54:27,233
Good job.

1375
00:54:27,563 --> 00:54:30,173
I'm sorry. Stay in there for just a while.

1376
00:54:32,203 --> 00:54:34,413
He can definitely go over the sofa, but he won't do that.

1377
00:54:34,513 --> 00:54:35,612
He never jumps over the sofa.

1378
00:54:35,613 --> 00:54:37,113
- He's smart. - He's smart.

1379
00:54:38,243 --> 00:54:41,453
(She returns to the kitchen after dealing with the situation.)

1380
00:54:42,953 --> 00:54:45,683
(She checks Bokdol's sweet potato.)

1381
00:54:46,853 --> 00:54:49,622
(Has it cooked well?)

1382
00:54:49,623 --> 00:54:50,953
Gosh, that's hot.

1383
00:54:51,623 --> 00:54:53,393
(The sweet potato was cooked just right.)

1384
00:54:54,693 --> 00:54:55,793
That's hot.

1385
00:54:56,063 --> 00:54:58,362
- So much care is put in. - Exactly.

1386
00:54:58,363 --> 00:55:00,403
- Dogs can't have hot things. - Right.

1387
00:55:01,033 --> 00:55:02,333
(Shaking)

1388
00:55:03,333 --> 00:55:04,603
- What are you adding in? - What is that?

1389
00:55:04,743 --> 00:55:07,342
- Is that a supplement? - He needs to take his medicine.

1390
00:55:07,343 --> 00:55:08,813
(Bokdol's medicine is added to Bokdol's favorite dried pollack.)

1391
00:55:09,273 --> 00:55:11,013
(Pouring)

1392
00:55:12,583 --> 00:55:15,883
(The cooled-down sweet potato is added as the finishing touch.)

1393
00:55:18,153 --> 00:55:20,353
(Sweating)

1394
00:55:21,393 --> 00:55:22,652
(Bokdol's special meal full of care is complete.)

1395
00:55:22,653 --> 00:55:24,663
How many meals is that for?

1396
00:55:25,263 --> 00:55:26,622
Does he eat that much for a single meal?

1397
00:55:26,623 --> 00:55:27,932
- It's for a single meal. - Gosh.

1398
00:55:27,933 --> 00:55:30,093
Isn't that too high in calories?

1399
00:55:30,163 --> 00:55:31,202
You have to feed him that much?

1400
00:55:31,203 --> 00:55:32,933
I was told he had to put on some weight.

1401
00:55:33,003 --> 00:55:34,973
That was why I cut up everything for him including the dried pollack.

1402
00:55:35,233 --> 00:55:37,703
He did put on some weight. He gained 2kg in a month and a half.

1403
00:55:38,173 --> 00:55:39,902
- His weight must be taken care of. - He must feel happy there...

1404
00:55:39,903 --> 00:55:41,073
as he gained weight.

1405
00:55:41,673 --> 00:55:42,743
That's a relief.

1406
00:55:43,773 --> 00:55:46,343
Bokdol.

1407
00:55:48,683 --> 00:55:49,683
Dried pollack?

1408
00:55:50,953 --> 00:55:52,052
(The dog from Mokpo gets excited after seeing the dried pollack.)

1409
00:55:52,053 --> 00:55:54,453
Gosh, you're so excited!

1410
00:55:55,753 --> 00:55:57,123
Have some water. Here.

1411
00:55:58,463 --> 00:56:00,493
The dog that loves dried pollack. Here you are.

1412
00:56:00,963 --> 00:56:03,232
(Eating)

1413
00:56:03,233 --> 00:56:04,463
Eat slowly.

1414
00:56:06,763 --> 00:56:07,802
Look at that.

1415
00:56:07,803 --> 00:56:08,803
- Gosh, he's eating well. - He's eating well.

1416
00:56:08,804 --> 00:56:10,273
He eats it so well.

1417
00:56:10,373 --> 00:56:12,703
Is it that good? There you go.

1418
00:56:13,943 --> 00:56:16,843
(He enjoys Na Rae's special meal.)

1419
00:56:17,783 --> 00:56:19,142
It feels great when the dog eats well, right?

1420
00:56:19,143 --> 00:56:20,842
- Right. - He eats well.

1421
00:56:20,843 --> 00:56:21,953
That's the best feeling.

1422
00:56:22,483 --> 00:56:25,283
(He eats for a while with his nose in the bowl.)

1423
00:56:25,423 --> 00:56:26,753
Let's see how much you have eaten.

1424
00:56:27,823 --> 00:56:30,153
Why did you leave the sweet potato? You ate all of the dried pollack.

1425
00:56:31,123 --> 00:56:32,393
Will you not finish the sweet potato?

1426
00:56:32,563 --> 00:56:33,963
He's definitely from Mokpo.

1427
00:56:34,633 --> 00:56:36,763
What a good dog. You ate well.

1428
00:56:38,263 --> 00:56:40,262
(Feeling drowsy)

1429
00:56:40,263 --> 00:56:41,403
- He must feel great. - Right.

1430
00:56:42,173 --> 00:56:44,773
(She returns to the kitchen after proudly feeding Bokdol.)

1431
00:56:45,073 --> 00:56:47,913
I don't know if I should eat or not.

1432
00:56:49,773 --> 00:56:50,773
It's like childrearing.

1433
00:56:50,774 --> 00:56:52,312
- Right. - Once I feed him,

1434
00:56:52,313 --> 00:56:54,483
- I'm completely exhausted. - Right.

1435
00:56:55,613 --> 00:56:57,853
(Rustling)

1436
00:56:58,053 --> 00:56:59,323
Low-sugar matcha.

1437
00:57:01,423 --> 00:57:02,892
(Let's eat lightly since I'm exhausted.)

1438
00:57:02,893 --> 00:57:05,222
I'm a true matcha lover.

1439
00:57:05,223 --> 00:57:06,363
Matcha lover.

1440
00:57:08,133 --> 00:57:11,403
(She prepares her meal after taking care of Bokdol.)

1441
00:57:15,903 --> 00:57:17,532
That's such a simple meal.

1442
00:57:17,533 --> 00:57:19,573
My life has become simple.

1443
00:57:20,743 --> 00:57:22,942
(Her breakfast was prepared in a flash.)

1444
00:57:22,943 --> 00:57:24,913
- You placed my paintings there. - Right.

1445
00:57:25,313 --> 00:57:26,943
That was the perfect spot.

1446
00:57:27,953 --> 00:57:29,483
I always see them there when I eat.

1447
00:57:31,253 --> 00:57:32,783
(Poking)

1448
00:57:34,183 --> 00:57:36,623
(She takes a big bite of the matcha rice cake.)

1449
00:57:37,593 --> 00:57:39,393
The matcha tastes rich.

1450
00:57:42,893 --> 00:57:45,963
(She enjoys a short break with the rice cake.)

1451
00:57:46,533 --> 00:57:48,673
(Satisfied)

1452
00:57:50,973 --> 00:57:52,943
There's so much filling inside.

1453
00:57:54,613 --> 00:57:55,913
This is the best in the morning.

1454
00:57:56,243 --> 00:57:57,712
(Eating)

1455
00:57:57,713 --> 00:58:00,442
You must eat your breakfast a lot simpler now.

1456
00:58:00,443 --> 00:58:01,552
I couldn't be bothered to do things now.

1457
00:58:01,553 --> 00:58:02,553
(I couldn't be bothered.)

1458
00:58:02,753 --> 00:58:05,322
That is why rookie parents don't eat well.

1459
00:58:05,323 --> 00:58:06,583
Right.

1460
00:58:14,863 --> 00:58:17,663
(The rookie dog owner moved busily early in the morning.)

1461
00:58:18,933 --> 00:58:20,063
Gosh.

1462
00:58:22,403 --> 00:58:24,943
(Her whole body aches.)

1463
00:58:27,003 --> 00:58:28,513
(She cleans up right away even though her body aches.)

1464
00:58:30,973 --> 00:58:33,113
Gosh, he didn't finish the sweet potato.

1465
00:58:33,183 --> 00:58:34,612
(She takes care of the leftovers.)

1466
00:58:34,613 --> 00:58:35,813
Well, someone has to take care of it.

1467
00:58:39,323 --> 00:58:41,023
I'll go and take a nap.

1468
00:58:43,353 --> 00:58:45,993
Right. Let's have some alone time.

1469
00:58:48,393 --> 00:58:50,833
(She goes back to her bed.)

1470
00:58:52,933 --> 00:58:54,503
As you got up too early?

1471
00:58:55,273 --> 00:58:57,433
I had to feed him.

1472
00:58:57,633 --> 00:58:59,842
I can't feed him at the time I usually wake up.

1473
00:58:59,843 --> 00:59:01,612
That is why I go back to sleep after feeding him.

1474
00:59:01,613 --> 00:59:02,642
You go back to sleep after doing everything?

1475
00:59:02,643 --> 00:59:03,673
Yes.

1476
00:59:04,743 --> 00:59:06,083
It's the same routine over and over.

1477
00:59:12,883 --> 00:59:13,883
(Groaning)

1478
00:59:16,693 --> 00:59:17,962
Gosh, I'm tired.

1479
00:59:17,963 --> 00:59:19,693
(Drowsy)

1480
00:59:20,623 --> 00:59:22,362
(She wakes up for the second time while struggling.)

1481
00:59:22,363 --> 00:59:24,663
- It's time to feed Bokdol lunch. - Right.

1482
00:59:26,333 --> 00:59:27,733
- You're the dog's mother. - Right.

1483
00:59:28,173 --> 00:59:29,802
- You then sleep again. - Right.

1484
00:59:29,803 --> 00:59:31,602
- And dinner is next. - Run the vacuum cleaner.

1485
00:59:31,603 --> 00:59:33,203
You're living a simpler life than a dog's life.

1486
00:59:34,403 --> 00:59:36,313
- The dog is busier. - Right.

1487
00:59:42,813 --> 00:59:43,883
Bokdol?

1488
00:59:44,553 --> 00:59:45,583
Bokdol?

1489
00:59:47,823 --> 00:59:48,852
Gosh!

1490
00:59:48,853 --> 00:59:49,993
(Smiling)

1491
00:59:50,753 --> 00:59:51,963
Did you get some rest?

1492
00:59:53,963 --> 00:59:56,362
Did you get some rest, sir?

1493
00:59:56,363 --> 00:59:57,392
(Reuniting with Bokdol as soon as she gets up)

1494
00:59:57,393 --> 01:00:00,163
Bokdol, did you get some rest?

1495
01:00:00,903 --> 01:00:02,103
How adorable.

1496
01:00:02,773 --> 01:00:04,572
You're so adorable.

1497
01:00:04,573 --> 01:00:06,373
- He likes that. - He does?

1498
01:00:06,743 --> 01:00:07,803
- Gosh. - He's like a cat.

1499
01:00:08,213 --> 01:00:10,743
- Oh, my. He's so cute. - That's amazing.

1500
01:00:11,173 --> 01:00:12,182
He doesn't even bark.

1501
01:00:12,183 --> 01:00:13,943
He doesn't like playing tug also.

1502
01:00:14,443 --> 01:00:15,553
But why doesn't he do it?

1503
01:00:15,653 --> 01:00:16,752
- I tried, - Yes.

1504
01:00:16,753 --> 01:00:19,183
- but because he's never done it... - It's because he's not used to it.

1505
01:00:19,583 --> 01:00:21,083
Maybe he finds toys boring.

1506
01:00:21,283 --> 01:00:22,452
He probably caught rats.

1507
01:00:22,453 --> 01:00:23,922
Should I have given him rats?

1508
01:00:23,923 --> 01:00:25,323
Right? Because...

1509
01:00:25,463 --> 01:00:28,162
he could've played more fiercely in the countryside.

1510
01:00:28,163 --> 01:00:29,463
The toy doesn't move around.

1511
01:00:31,333 --> 01:00:33,333
You should let loose a few rats, then.

1512
01:00:33,463 --> 01:00:34,902
I should let loose a few rats at home?

1513
01:00:34,903 --> 01:00:36,433
(Kian84's solution)

1514
01:00:37,373 --> 01:00:38,473
Bokdol.

1515
01:00:40,043 --> 01:00:41,173
Shall we wear new clothes?

1516
01:00:42,773 --> 01:00:44,043
Do you want a necklace?

1517
01:00:44,243 --> 01:00:46,143
Okay? Hold on a second.

1518
01:00:50,353 --> 01:00:52,083
Bokdol, stay still. Wait.

1519
01:00:53,083 --> 01:00:54,153
Wait.

1520
01:00:55,153 --> 01:00:56,253
Good job.

1521
01:00:58,363 --> 01:01:00,923
I just said he did well from my perspective.

1522
01:01:01,063 --> 01:01:02,163
- He likes it. - Yes.

1523
01:01:03,763 --> 01:01:05,463
Bokdol, were you waiting?

1524
01:01:05,603 --> 01:01:06,762
Goodness. Here we go.

1525
01:01:06,763 --> 01:01:08,072
- He should be complimented. - You should compliment him.

1526
01:01:08,073 --> 01:01:10,633
- You need to reward him a lot. - Yes, you need to reward him now.

1527
01:01:12,773 --> 01:01:13,802
Bokdol.

1528
01:01:13,803 --> 01:01:14,813
(Since he did well, I should reward him.)

1529
01:01:15,313 --> 01:01:16,443
Bokdol, shall we put this on?

1530
01:01:16,673 --> 01:01:18,513
Shall we put this on?

1531
01:01:18,743 --> 01:01:21,083
That's what you do when you first get a dog.

1532
01:01:21,883 --> 01:01:22,983
What do you think?

1533
01:01:23,653 --> 01:01:25,083
A cynical man in Itaewon.

1534
01:01:26,183 --> 01:01:27,682
A cynical man in Itaewon.

1535
01:01:27,683 --> 01:01:28,792
(Not interested)

1536
01:01:28,793 --> 01:01:29,893
He doesn't like it.

1537
01:01:29,993 --> 01:01:31,393
Goodness, that boy.

1538
01:01:32,363 --> 01:01:34,562
Now that Bokdol is living...

1539
01:01:34,563 --> 01:01:38,363
in Itaewon, which is right in the middle of Seoul,

1540
01:01:38,763 --> 01:01:40,033
I'd like it...

1541
01:01:40,603 --> 01:01:43,002
- if he becomes stylish. - He's handsome.

1542
01:01:43,003 --> 01:01:44,033
Yes.

1543
01:01:44,943 --> 01:01:46,042
(The fashionista dogs are just as stylish as their owners.)

1544
01:01:46,043 --> 01:01:47,142
They're so cute!

1545
01:01:47,143 --> 01:01:48,813
Yes, just like that.

1546
01:01:49,173 --> 01:01:50,273
Zero.

1547
01:01:50,943 --> 01:01:54,042
I was hoping Bokdol would be reborn.

1548
01:01:54,043 --> 01:01:56,083
Yes! He should dress this fancy.

1549
01:01:56,253 --> 01:01:58,013
I bought a lot of clothes for him.

1550
01:01:58,523 --> 01:02:00,922
Maybe he can fit your clothes.

1551
01:02:00,923 --> 01:02:01,993
Roughly, yes.

1552
01:02:02,393 --> 01:02:04,792
I think he can do it.

1553
01:02:04,793 --> 01:02:05,793
(If it's my Bokdol, he's more than capable.)

1554
01:02:06,493 --> 01:02:09,293
(I'll make you a stylish dog!)

1555
01:02:09,933 --> 01:02:11,933
Let me see. How pretty!

1556
01:02:12,403 --> 01:02:13,433
Let me see.

1557
01:02:14,233 --> 01:02:15,302
You're a flower dog.

1558
01:02:15,303 --> 01:02:18,202
