- They don't listen to their moms. - That's right.

1812
01:11:18,413 --> 01:11:19,912
They only get mad because their mothers are easy.

1813
01:11:19,913 --> 01:11:21,443
- That's right. - "What have you ever done for me?"

1814
01:11:21,513 --> 01:11:22,852
(Feeling guilty)

1815
01:11:22,853 --> 01:11:25,153
Then the mothers will be, "What more can I do?"

1816
01:11:26,183 --> 01:11:27,653
(You must've heard that often.)

1817
01:11:28,223 --> 01:11:29,753
- What should I do now? - All right.

1818
01:11:30,053 --> 01:11:32,522
Now, we need to use the power of treats...

1819
01:11:32,523 --> 01:11:33,722
because he loves treats.

1820
01:11:33,723 --> 01:11:36,563
Put all these treats in your pocket.

1821
01:11:37,463 --> 01:11:39,362
You have the treats,

1822
01:11:39,363 --> 01:11:41,202
and she has an empty bowl.

1823
01:11:41,203 --> 01:11:44,073
Bokdol will get the treat only when he goes to you.

1824
01:11:44,233 --> 01:11:45,443
All right. Sit down.

1825
01:11:46,203 --> 01:11:47,802
You should come here too.

1826
01:11:47,803 --> 01:11:48,973
Bokdol.

1827
01:11:49,473 --> 01:11:50,543
Bokdol.

1828
01:11:51,013 --> 01:11:52,212
Bokdol.

1829
01:11:52,213 --> 01:11:53,343
That's fascinating.

1830
01:11:53,743 --> 01:11:54,812
Bokdol.

1831
01:11:54,813 --> 01:11:56,182
I'm not tempting him with treats.

1832
01:11:56,183 --> 01:11:58,012
We're training him to come to me with my voice only.

1833
01:11:58,013 --> 01:11:59,052
Bokdol.

1834
01:11:59,053 --> 01:12:01,022
So your position will be higher than the treats.

1835
01:12:01,023 --> 01:12:02,153
- That's right. - Yes.

1836
01:12:02,493 --> 01:12:05,123
(Will it be treats or Na Rae?)

1837
01:12:06,123 --> 01:12:07,522
(Which will Bokdol choose?)

1838
01:12:07,523 --> 01:12:08,693
(Bokdol?)

1839
01:12:09,693 --> 01:12:10,933
Bokdol.

1840
01:12:11,193 --> 01:12:13,162
- "Good job." Give him a treat. - Goodness.

1841
01:12:13,163 --> 01:12:15,232
Good job. There you go.

1842
01:12:15,233 --> 01:12:17,603
Move to another spot, Na Rae.

1843
01:12:18,273 --> 01:12:20,043
Trainer, move to another spot too.

1844
01:12:20,703 --> 01:12:21,803
Bokdol.

1845
01:12:22,773 --> 01:12:24,143
(Clattering)

1846
01:12:24,213 --> 01:12:26,012
(Gosh, isn't that my bowl?)

1847
01:12:26,013 --> 01:12:27,342
Na Rae, call him.

1848
01:12:27,343 --> 01:12:28,413
Bokdol.

1849
01:12:28,643 --> 01:12:29,883
Bokdol.

1850
01:12:30,753 --> 01:12:32,152
There's no treat when someone else calls him.

1851
01:12:32,153 --> 01:12:33,253
Bokdol.

1852
01:12:33,523 --> 01:12:36,123
(He comes close to Na Rae again.)

1853
01:12:36,323 --> 01:12:38,822
- Goodness. Good job. - All right.

1854
01:12:38,823 --> 01:12:40,563
- No, don't touch him. - No?

1855
01:12:41,293 --> 01:12:42,663
Push and pull!

1856
01:12:43,063 --> 01:12:45,193
- All right. - Give him a treat only.

1857
01:12:45,333 --> 01:12:48,303
It could be a similar stimulation for Bokdol.

1858
01:12:48,403 --> 01:12:51,573
But only his owner gets a chance to reward him.

1859
01:12:52,003 --> 01:12:53,072
Oh, it's gaslighting?

1860
01:12:53,073 --> 01:12:54,903
- In a good way. - Yes, in a good way.

1861
01:12:55,073 --> 01:12:57,073
Let's try that a few more times.

1862
01:12:58,013 --> 01:12:59,712
This will turn into play.

1863
01:12:59,713 --> 01:13:00,782
(Sitting in a corner like they're playing hide-and-seek)

1864
01:13:00,783 --> 01:13:01,843
Bokdol.

1865
01:13:02,883 --> 01:13:05,622
- "Good job." - Good job.

1866
01:13:05,623 --> 01:13:07,282
- It looks like it's working. - Yes, it is.

1867
01:13:07,283 --> 01:13:08,453
- Right? - It works now.

1868
01:13:09,153 --> 01:13:10,753
(Sitting here and there without a break)

1869
01:13:11,293 --> 01:13:12,563
Bokdol.

1870
01:13:13,593 --> 01:13:16,133
- Must you sit like that? - Yes, I had to.

1871
01:13:16,793 --> 01:13:18,232
- It's hot, right? - Yes.

1872
01:13:18,233 --> 01:13:19,933
She's sweating.

1873
01:13:20,063 --> 01:13:22,632
(Pitiful)

1874
01:13:22,633 --> 01:13:25,233
Maybe he won't listen to you if you don't sit like that.

1875
01:13:26,573 --> 01:13:27,943
Bokdol.

1876
01:13:28,303 --> 01:13:30,313
(You're sitting there.)

1877
01:13:30,443 --> 01:13:32,073
Bokdol?

1878
01:13:32,513 --> 01:13:33,742
You should crouch down with your back against him...

1879
01:13:33,743 --> 01:13:34,983
even when you're outside.

1880
01:13:36,253 --> 01:13:38,513
- Bokdol. - He'll only look for your back.

1881
01:13:38,683 --> 01:13:40,422
- Bokdol. - You did it for quite a long time.

1882
01:13:40,423 --> 01:13:43,323
- We did it for an hour. - Well done. Good job.

1883
01:13:43,853 --> 01:13:45,122
- You did it for a long time. - I don't know...

1884
01:13:45,123 --> 01:13:46,563
if I'm training him or myself.

1885
01:13:47,963 --> 01:13:49,663
(Sweaty)

1886
01:13:50,393 --> 01:13:53,663
- Say, "Good job." - Good job.

1887
01:13:54,133 --> 01:13:55,603
You did well today.

1888
01:13:56,673 --> 01:13:57,932
It's to make him come to you when you call...

1889
01:13:57,933 --> 01:13:59,173
even if you don't have treats.

1890
01:13:59,243 --> 01:14:00,942
For that to happen, you need to repeat this a lot.

1891
01:14:00,943 --> 01:14:02,312
It's not easy.

1892
01:14:02,313 --> 01:14:03,713
It certainly is not.

1893
01:14:03,973 --> 01:14:05,613
- We'll get going now. - Okay.

1894
01:14:06,243 --> 01:14:08,243
Bokdol. Stay here for a second.

1895
01:14:10,053 --> 01:14:11,452
(Na Rae came out after getting changed?)

1896
01:14:11,453 --> 01:14:12,523
What is this now?

1897
01:14:12,623 --> 01:14:14,083
Bokdol, shall we go for a walk?

1898
01:14:14,523 --> 01:14:15,622
I'll open it for you.

1899
01:14:15,623 --> 01:14:16,752
- He likes it. - Let's go.

1900
01:14:16,753 --> 01:14:18,792
- He knows what walking is. - I'll open the door for you.

1901
01:14:18,793 --> 01:14:19,892
Dogs know you're going out...

1902
01:14:19,893 --> 01:14:20,962
- when you get changed. - Let's go.

1903
01:14:20,963 --> 01:14:22,993
- Dudu knows. - I see.

1904
01:14:23,233 --> 01:14:24,863
I need to pack for walking.

1905
01:14:25,963 --> 01:14:27,102
(Feeling the best)

1906
01:14:27,103 --> 01:14:29,303
They go ecstatic when you pack things.

1907
01:14:29,603 --> 01:14:31,633
(Getting ready to walk Bokdol even though she's tired)

1908
01:14:32,173 --> 01:14:33,643
Wet wipes...

1909
01:14:33,803 --> 01:14:35,003
and poop bag.

1910
01:14:35,243 --> 01:14:36,272
And my bullets.

1911
01:14:36,273 --> 01:14:37,313
(Getting lots of treats)

1912
01:14:38,013 --> 01:14:39,143
My flower dog.

1913
01:14:40,343 --> 01:14:41,512
Come here.

1914
01:14:41,513 --> 01:14:43,483
Let's put this on before we leave.

1915
01:14:44,153 --> 01:14:45,653
- There you go. - He's so gentle.

1916
01:14:46,523 --> 01:14:49,292
How cute!

1917
01:14:49,293 --> 01:14:52,363
Bokdol. You're so cute.

1918
01:14:52,893 --> 01:14:54,223
You're so cute, Bokdol.

1919
01:14:54,793 --> 01:14:56,462
I look like a helicopter mom.

1920
01:14:56,463 --> 01:14:58,692
Bokdol.

1921
01:14:58,693 --> 01:15:00,562
Let's go. Let's go out.

1922
01:15:00,563 --> 01:15:02,133
(Helicopter sister goes for a walk as soon as the training is over.)

1923
01:15:03,773 --> 01:15:05,172
(Bokdol goes ahead as he's excited.)

1924
01:15:05,173 --> 01:15:06,603
He walks well.

1925
01:15:06,903 --> 01:15:08,642
(The dog from Mokpo is excited with the smell of Seoul.)

1926
01:15:08,643 --> 01:15:09,743
Bokdol.

1927
01:15:10,143 --> 01:15:12,513
Let's go use the stairs.

1928
01:15:13,413 --> 01:15:14,982
(Hesitating)

1929
01:15:14,983 --> 01:15:16,783
- They're scared of that at first. - Let's use the stairs.

1930
01:15:17,883 --> 01:15:18,953
Bokdol, let's go up.

1931
01:15:19,883 --> 01:15:21,952
- Bokdol, come up. - But he uses the stairs at home.

1932
01:15:21,953 --> 01:15:23,792
- He can't use different stairs. - I know.

1933
01:15:23,793 --> 01:15:24,892
(Hiding behind Na Rae as he's scared)

1934
01:15:24,893 --> 01:15:25,893
Come up.

1935
01:15:26,363 --> 01:15:28,463
Bokdol. Look.

1936
01:15:29,163 --> 01:15:31,433
(Na Rae calmly waits for him.)

1937
01:15:32,193 --> 01:15:33,262
Come up.

1938
01:15:33,263 --> 01:15:34,702
(Trust me and come up.)

1939
01:15:34,703 --> 01:15:37,732
There you go! Good job.

1940
01:15:37,733 --> 01:15:38,873
Good job.

1941
01:15:39,303 --> 01:15:41,603
Good job. Bokdol.

1942
01:15:41,743 --> 01:15:43,443
(Bokdol has become a lot braver.)

1943
01:15:43,713 --> 01:15:45,272
(Since he did a good job, he gets a treat right away.)

1944
01:15:45,273 --> 01:15:46,743
- How cute. - You're awesome.

1945
01:15:47,013 --> 01:15:48,813
He's lucky when it comes to food.

1946
01:15:49,213 --> 01:15:51,012
There you go!

1947
01:15:51,013 --> 01:15:52,053
(Surprised)

1948
01:15:52,883 --> 01:15:56,223
There you go! Good job.

1949
01:15:56,323 --> 01:15:58,423
- Goodness. - Look at you.

1950
01:15:58,753 --> 01:16:00,992
(My baby is so brave.)

1951
01:16:00,993 --> 01:16:02,793
Bokdol. Good job.

1952
01:16:03,293 --> 01:16:04,363
You did well.

1953
01:16:04,633 --> 01:16:07,402
Those who have dogs say, "There you go" a lot.

1954
01:16:07,403 --> 01:16:09,002
- We do. "There you go. Good job." - That's right.

1955
01:16:09,003 --> 01:16:11,232
I have a friend who moved to Canada,

1956
01:16:11,233 --> 01:16:13,172
and their dog knows "There you go" in Korean.

1957
01:16:13,173 --> 01:16:14,272
A Canadian dog?

1958
01:16:14,273 --> 01:16:16,712
- "There you go." - "There you go."

1959
01:16:16,713 --> 01:16:19,042
- Because they say it a lot. - "There you go."

1960
01:16:19,043 --> 01:16:20,642
He couldn't climb up those stairs the day before.

1961
01:16:20,643 --> 01:16:22,013
So I carried him.

1962
01:16:22,283 --> 01:16:24,183
(A genius dog who overcame the unfriendly stairs in a day)

1963
01:16:24,553 --> 01:16:25,852
(They keep walking excitedly.)

1964
01:16:25,853 --> 01:16:27,083
All right.

1965
01:16:27,253 --> 01:16:28,752
There you go.

1966
01:16:28,753 --> 01:16:29,923
(The helicopter sister bombards him with compliments.)

1967
01:16:29,993 --> 01:16:32,152
- Why do you like grass so much? - My dogs do too.

1968
01:16:32,153 --> 01:16:34,193
Dogs love grass.

1969
01:16:34,893 --> 01:16:37,033
(Na Rae, hurry up.)

1970
01:16:37,693 --> 01:16:39,332
He loves all the grass in the neighborhood.

1971
01:16:39,333 --> 01:16:40,963
Why does he like it so much?

1972
01:16:42,103 --> 01:16:43,832
(I want to understand you.)

1973
01:16:43,833 --> 01:16:45,503
(Sniffing)

1974
01:16:45,633 --> 01:16:46,703
- I was curious. - He likes this smell?

1975
01:16:50,373 --> 01:16:52,112
(Releasing a waterfall on top of Na Rae's scent)

1976
01:16:52,113 --> 01:16:53,183
Dog marking.

1977
01:16:55,283 --> 01:16:56,413
All right.

1978
01:16:58,253 --> 01:16:59,983
Please hold.

1979
01:17:00,123 --> 01:17:02,122
There you go.

1980
01:17:02,123 --> 01:17:03,353
Gosh, how cute.

1981
01:17:03,793 --> 01:17:05,792
There you go. You're doing so well.

1982
01:17:05,793 --> 01:17:07,763
(She's proud of everything he does.)

1983
01:17:08,393 --> 01:17:09,793
(Startled)

1984
01:17:10,393 --> 01:17:11,632
You're scared of people.

1985
01:17:11,633 --> 01:17:14,062
You're scared of cars.

1986
01:17:14,063 --> 01:17:17,173
There are barely any cars near Grandma's place.

1987
01:17:17,433 --> 01:17:19,073
So he's scared of roads.

1988
01:17:19,273 --> 01:17:20,302
(Patting)

1989
01:17:20,303 --> 01:17:21,403
Let's go.

1990
01:17:23,013 --> 01:17:24,642
Let's hurry up and cross.

1991
01:17:24,643 --> 01:17:26,243
- Goodness. - You're doing so well.

1992
01:17:27,543 --> 01:17:28,842
Where shall we go?

1993
01:17:28,843 --> 01:17:30,313
This way? Okay, let's go this way.

1994
01:17:30,913 --> 01:17:32,582
(Namsan Seoul Tower)

1995
01:17:32,583 --> 01:17:34,222
Gosh, you went to a good place.

1996
01:17:34,223 --> 01:17:35,552
This is the best spot.

1997
01:17:35,553 --> 01:17:38,423
(A place where various kinds of dogs gather)

1998
01:17:39,463 --> 01:17:41,723
(A place where dogs socialize)

1999
01:17:42,193 --> 01:17:43,762
I should have a dog gathering someday.

2000
01:17:43,763 --> 01:17:45,333
- I know. - It's so cool.

2001
01:17:48,763 --> 01:17:50,803
(Getting dragged)

2002
01:17:51,203 --> 01:17:52,403
Do you want to run?

2003
01:17:52,973 --> 01:17:54,102
Shall we run?

2004
01:17:54,103 --> 01:17:55,673
(If Bokdol wants to run...)

2005
01:17:56,073 --> 01:17:57,713
Let's run.

2006
01:17:59,813 --> 01:18:01,112
Run!

2007
01:18:01,113 --> 01:18:02,452
(Bokdol runs excitedly.)

2008
01:18:02,453 --> 01:18:04,153
- He runs well. - Let's run. There you go.

2009
01:18:04,653 --> 01:18:06,353
Gosh. Slow down.

2010
01:18:07,223 --> 01:18:09,193
Come here.

2011
01:18:09,323 --> 01:18:11,793
Let's drink water.

2012
01:18:13,063 --> 01:18:14,293
It's tiring, right?

2013
01:18:14,523 --> 01:18:16,393
Bokdol, it's tiring.

2014
01:18:16,493 --> 01:18:17,593
(Smiling)

2015
01:18:20,203 --> 01:18:21,703
I think you need to drink water.

2016
01:18:21,903 --> 01:18:23,073
That's right. I was tired.

2017
01:18:23,733 --> 01:18:24,833
I don't have strength.

2018
01:18:28,073 --> 01:18:29,143
Bokdol.

2019
01:18:29,813 --> 01:18:30,873
Have some water.

2020
01:18:31,473 --> 01:18:34,082
That's a bowl for makgeolli, right?

2021
01:18:34,083 --> 01:18:35,382
- I'll give you water. - He only drinks water...

2022
01:18:35,383 --> 01:18:36,452
from a wide bowl.

2023
01:18:36,453 --> 01:18:37,913
Bokdol is used to that.

2024
01:18:39,223 --> 01:18:41,582
(Lapping up)

2025
01:18:41,583 --> 01:18:45,453
What is it? Water. Drink water.

2026
01:18:45,923 --> 01:18:48,223
Bokdol, water.

2027
01:18:48,923 --> 01:18:50,932
Come here. Have water.

2028
01:18:50,933 --> 01:18:52,762
If he's really thirsty, he'll drink on his own.

2029
01:18:52,763 --> 01:18:53,963
- Is that so? - Have water.

2030
01:18:54,603 --> 01:18:56,603
Have water. You don't want it?

2031
01:18:57,533 --> 01:18:58,702
You don't want it?

2032
01:18:58,703 --> 01:18:59,703
(Why won't he drink water?)

2033
01:19:02,173 --> 01:19:05,043
(Throwing the water out and resuming walking)

2034
01:19:05,813 --> 01:19:08,283
Slow down. Go slowly.

2035
01:19:09,313 --> 01:19:11,653
No. Oh, my.

2036
01:19:12,153 --> 01:19:13,383
No.

2037
01:19:13,653 --> 01:19:16,322
- It's him. No. - My goodness.

2038
01:19:16,323 --> 01:19:17,423
No.

2039
01:19:17,853 --> 01:19:18,892
(Moving up and down)

2040
01:19:18,893 --> 01:19:20,963
No. You're scared.

2041
01:19:21,523 --> 01:19:24,033
- Bokdol, come here. - No, he doesn't seem scared.

2042
01:19:24,833 --> 01:19:25,863
Really?

2043
01:19:26,303 --> 01:19:27,732
You're scared. It's okay.

2044
01:19:27,733 --> 01:19:29,473
I'm here. Come here.

2045
01:19:29,973 --> 01:19:31,273
Look how fast your heart is beating.

2046
01:19:31,973 --> 01:19:33,073
Oh, my.

2047
01:19:33,173 --> 01:19:34,502
- I think you are scared. - You're scared.

2048
01:19:34,503 --> 01:19:35,642
Yes, I was scared. You're right.

2049
01:19:35,643 --> 01:19:37,873
All right. Let's go.

2050
01:19:40,613 --> 01:19:42,513
(Sweating profusely)

2051
01:19:45,713 --> 01:19:47,022
You'd lose weight.

2052
01:19:47,023 --> 01:19:48,023
- I did. - Exactly.

2053
01:19:48,024 --> 01:19:49,393
I did lose some weight.

2054
01:19:50,393 --> 01:19:52,293
(He's just bright.)

2055
01:19:56,163 --> 01:19:58,233
No. You can't.

2056
01:20:00,233 --> 01:20:01,332
Stay here.

2057
01:20:01,333 --> 01:20:02,732
(Trying her best to protect him)

2058
01:20:02,733 --> 01:20:04,802
- Is someone coming? - Stay with me.

2059
01:20:04,803 --> 01:20:06,643
- It's coming. - A big dog is coming.

2060
01:20:07,743 --> 01:20:09,003
- It's not big. - No.

2061
01:20:09,513 --> 01:20:11,242
What is it? Oh, there's a dog?

2062
01:20:11,243 --> 01:20:13,083
(Trotting)

2063
01:20:13,583 --> 01:20:16,082
Bokdol, that dog is four times smaller than you.

2064
01:20:16,083 --> 01:20:18,712
It's not scary. You brat, you're such a scaredy-cat.

2065
01:20:18,713 --> 01:20:20,353
What do we do?

2066
01:20:20,623 --> 01:20:22,353
Look. You're so scared.

2067
01:20:22,483 --> 01:20:24,693
- I think he's curious. - It's okay.

2068
01:20:24,923 --> 01:20:26,592
I don't think you need to...

2069
01:20:26,593 --> 01:20:27,862
- block him that much. - Let's go.

2070
01:20:27,863 --> 01:20:29,393
Is that so? Did I get too ahead?

2071
01:20:29,793 --> 01:20:32,763
I feel like you're rather making him mad.

2072
01:20:33,433 --> 01:20:35,102
You tell him to hold it,

2073
01:20:35,103 --> 01:20:36,372
- "What's wrong with her?" - so he gets mad.

2074
01:20:36,373 --> 01:20:38,502
- "Let go of me!" - Oh, no.

2075
01:20:38,503 --> 01:20:40,072
He won't go if you let go.

2076
01:20:40,073 --> 01:20:41,203
That's right.

2077
01:20:42,173 --> 01:20:44,743
Let's go. Let's go home and rest.

2078
01:20:45,043 --> 01:20:46,842
You stayed out for quite a long time.

2079
01:20:46,843 --> 01:20:48,113
I walked for an hour.

2080
01:20:49,353 --> 01:20:51,352
Bokdol, stay here for a second.

2081
01:20:51,353 --> 01:20:52,723
(They came home after walking.)

2082
01:20:53,523 --> 01:20:55,583
Hold on. We need to wipe your feet.

2083
01:20:56,023 --> 01:20:58,423
Come here.

2084
01:21:00,263 --> 01:21:01,323
Good work.

2085
01:21:03,633 --> 01:21:04,893
I'll remove this.

2086
01:21:05,563 --> 01:21:06,803
You can't eat it anymore.

2087
01:21:07,033 --> 01:21:08,703
Sweet potatoes, dried pollack.

2088
01:21:09,933 --> 01:21:10,933
You're banned.

2089
01:21:10,934 --> 01:21:12,273
(Removing it right away as she learned)

2090
01:21:12,943 --> 01:21:14,803
(Disappointed)

2091
01:21:15,943 --> 01:21:18,573
Get some rest. You should rest, and so should I.

2092
01:21:21,713 --> 01:21:22,813
Gosh, I'm starved.

2093
01:21:23,053 --> 01:21:24,212
It was 4pm.

2094
01:21:24,213 --> 01:21:25,812
All I had before that were two pieces of rice cake.

2095
01:21:25,813 --> 01:21:27,052
You must be starving.

2096
01:21:27,053 --> 01:21:28,353
She only had two pieces of rice cake.

2097
01:21:30,853 --> 01:21:34,393
(Let me see. This...)

2098
01:21:35,893 --> 01:21:37,963
It's Bokdol's favorite, dried pollack.

2099
01:21:38,533 --> 01:21:39,732
(I should eat it.)

2100
01:21:39,733 --> 01:21:41,802
- You're eating it? - She's eating it herself?

2101
01:21:41,803 --> 01:21:43,373
She told me not to feed him,

2102
01:21:43,903 --> 01:21:44,932
so I have to finish it.

2103
01:21:44,933 --> 01:21:47,242
- Only you can cook like that. - That's right.

2104
01:21:47,243 --> 01:21:49,373
If it was someone else, they'd have ordered in.

2105
01:21:51,113 --> 01:21:53,483
He smelled it.

2106
01:21:54,213 --> 01:21:56,613
(Pouring an abundant amount of perilla oil)

2107
01:21:57,683 --> 01:22:00,382
(Pouring water...)

2108
01:22:00,383 --> 01:22:01,883
(and adding an egg)

2109
01:22:03,253 --> 01:22:05,023
(Dried pollack soup is ready in no time.)

2110
01:22:05,793 --> 01:22:08,192
It's the simplest meal I've seen from you.

2111
01:22:08,193 --> 01:22:09,832
It really was simple.

2112
01:22:09,833 --> 01:22:11,263
One might think you're on a diet.

2113
01:22:11,733 --> 01:22:13,233
(While Bokdol is resting)

2114
01:22:15,233 --> 01:22:17,003
(I should eat it quickly.)

2115
01:22:20,673 --> 01:22:22,373
(Taking a bite of the steaming dried pollack soup)

2116
01:22:25,773 --> 01:22:26,983
Dried pollack is delicious.

2117
01:22:27,943 --> 01:22:29,142
No wonder he loves it.

2118
01:22:29,143 --> 01:22:30,653
(No wonder Bokdol loves it.)

2119
01:22:31,753 --> 01:22:34,723
(Eating in a hurry)

2120
01:22:36,053 --> 01:22:39,093
(It feels like her fatigue is washed away.)

2121
01:22:39,663 --> 01:22:43,393
(Slurping)

2122
01:22:45,833 --> 01:22:46,862
(This time, with kimchi on top)

2123
01:22:46,863 --> 01:22:48,233
It must be so good.

2124
01:22:50,033 --> 01:22:52,473
(Getting ready)

2125
01:22:53,303 --> 01:22:55,103
I just ate it even if it burned my throat.

2126
01:22:55,273 --> 01:22:56,442
Because you were hungry.

2127
01:22:56,443 --> 01:22:58,242
It looks like a mother eating what her child left.

2128
01:22:58,243 --> 01:23:00,043
Yes, like the kid's leftovers.

2129
01:23:00,543 --> 01:23:04,313
(Eating in a hurry after taking care of her child)

2130
01:23:05,083 --> 01:23:06,783
(Bokdol's sister eats the dried pollack instead of him)

2131
01:23:08,583 --> 01:23:09,923
I bought so much dried pollack, though.

2132
01:23:11,253 --> 01:23:12,393
This is bad.

2133
01:23:12,693 --> 01:23:13,693
(Slurping)

2134
01:23:14,093 --> 01:23:15,093
(Munching)

2135
01:23:19,703 --> 01:23:21,062
(With worries,)

2136
01:23:21,063 --> 01:23:24,373
(she drinks it from the bowl with her spoon down.)

2137
01:23:26,843 --> 01:23:29,303
(I can finally breathe.)

2138
01:23:29,513 --> 01:23:30,643
Oh, right. Sweet potatoes.

2139
01:23:32,413 --> 01:23:33,643
You're going to eat that too?

2140
01:23:35,983 --> 01:23:38,352
(Peeling a sweet potato with care)

2141
01:23:38,353 --> 01:23:39,623
(Tapping)

2142
01:23:40,423 --> 01:23:41,483
Bokdol.

2143
01:23:42,323 --> 01:23:44,093
Give sweet potatoes only when you give him medicine.

2144
01:23:44,923 --> 01:23:47,223
Gosh, it's hot. It must be good, right?

2145
01:23:47,393 --> 01:23:49,162
Yes. Let's eat.

2146
01:23:49,163 --> 01:23:51,733
Goodness. You're eating so well.

2147
01:23:53,763 --> 01:23:56,232
Yes, eat up.

2148
01:23:56,233 --> 01:23:59,272
(Na Rae watches Bokdol until the end so he has his medicine.)

2149
01:23:59,273 --> 01:24:00,373
I don't have any more.

2150
01:24:02,673 --> 01:24:05,212
It feels like I got a friend...

2151
01:24:05,213 --> 01:24:07,213
who will trust me until the end. I felt really good.

2152
01:24:07,583 --> 01:24:10,512
We're not super close yet,

2153
01:24:10,513 --> 01:24:12,882
but we have a great chance of becoming close friends.

2154
01:24:12,883 --> 01:24:13,922
She's amazing.

2155
01:24:13,923 --> 01:24:15,323
(Bokdol and me)

2156
01:24:15,623 --> 01:24:18,092
We're at a stage where we...

2157
01:24:18,093 --> 01:24:20,523
learn about each other little by little.

2158
01:24:21,423 --> 01:24:24,163
The things Bokdol's never done and what I've never done.

2159
01:24:24,393 --> 01:24:26,332
We'll make good memories,

2160
01:24:26,333 --> 01:24:27,603
and I feel like...

2161
01:24:28,503 --> 01:24:30,473
the days we'll share together will be fun.

2162
01:24:30,833 --> 01:24:32,303
I think he's the same as me.

2163
01:24:33,073 --> 01:24:34,873
I sprawl on the floor like this when I'm drunk.

2164
01:24:35,273 --> 01:24:36,373
We're the same.

2165
01:24:36,713 --> 01:24:37,713
Look.

2166
01:24:38,873 --> 01:24:40,243
I thought it was a human.

2167
01:24:40,343 --> 01:24:41,883
That's when you're lying on the grass.

2168
01:24:43,183 --> 01:24:44,652
- Gosh, look at him. - He sleeps well.

2169
01:24:44,653 --> 01:24:45,882
He does sleep well.

2170
01:24:45,883 --> 01:24:48,283
- He let his guard down. - He's hardly wary now.

2171
01:24:49,723 --> 01:24:51,922
Let's live well together in our house.

2172
01:24:51,923 --> 01:24:53,892
(Bokdol, let's live well together in our house.)

2173
01:24:53,893 --> 01:24:55,963
In any case,

2174
01:24:56,963 --> 01:24:58,992
you should consider this place your home.

2175
01:24:58,993 --> 01:25:00,962
(Bokdol, this is your home now.)

2176
01:25:00,963 --> 01:25:02,733
Itaewon is your home now.

2177
01:25:04,073 --> 01:25:06,273
Who knew a dog would live in that house?

2178
01:25:06,473 --> 01:25:08,243
I became really stable.

2179
01:25:09,243 --> 01:25:12,072
Let's show Grandma and Grandpa that we're living well together.

2180
01:25:12,073 --> 01:25:14,342
(Let's show Grandma and Grandpa that we're living well together.)

2181
01:25:14,343 --> 01:25:15,383
Okay?

2182
01:25:17,083 --> 01:25:18,382
(It's a Little Rough, but It's Okay)

2183
01:25:18,383 --> 01:25:19,383
How cute.

2184
01:25:20,953 --> 01:25:22,423
(Next story)

2185
01:25:23,823 --> 01:25:25,893
(Sung Hwan's eyes are filled with love.)

2186
01:25:26,493 --> 01:25:27,993
(Kkotbun is right by his side as always.)

2187
01:25:29,123 --> 01:25:31,133
(Looking at each other with affection)

2188
01:25:32,363 --> 01:25:33,703
(Therapeutic walking time)

2189
01:25:34,433 --> 01:25:36,533
(This is the park Sung Hwan and Kkotbun come often.)

2190
01:25:37,233 --> 01:25:38,773
(I'm excited!)

2191
01:25:39,403 --> 01:25:41,543
(Gosh, you look like a dog I'd grow fond of.)

2192
01:25:42,603 --> 01:25:43,913
(Who are you?)

2193
01:25:44,313 --> 01:25:45,513
(Kissing)

2194
01:25:46,543 --> 01:25:47,783
(Sung Hwan, what about me?)

2195
01:25:48,343 --> 01:25:50,013
(Sung Hwan is absorbed in new dogs.)

2196
01:25:50,553 --> 01:25:52,283
(She looks super angry from behind.)

2197
01:25:53,083 --> 01:25:54,253
(Trying her best to look away)

2198
01:25:55,823 --> 01:25:57,453
(But you're the best, Kkotbun.)

2199
01:25:58,223 --> 01:26:01,062
(The person he met after soothing Kkotbun)

2200
01:26:01,063 --> 01:26:02,593
(It's Ju Seung's mother?)

2201
01:26:03,693 --> 01:26:06,063
(Ju Seung's mother has taken good care of Sung Hwan.)

2202
01:26:06,903 --> 01:26:09,803
(She prepared a gift for him as expected.)

2203
01:26:10,303 --> 01:26:11,833
(Thank you so much, Mom.)

2204
01:26:12,273 --> 01:26:15,203
(And one by one, people gather.)

2205
01:26:16,043 --> 01:26:18,143
(The precious friends he got to meet thanks to Ju Seung)

2206
01:26:18,573 --> 01:26:21,643
(Chatting happily and cozily)

2207
01:26:23,483 --> 01:26:24,583
(Look at Sung Hwan carefully.)

2208
01:26:25,153 --> 01:26:26,823
(To the mother, Sung Hwan is incredibly cute.)

2209
01:26:27,823 --> 01:26:30,123
(Everything else goes along well except for your eyes.)

2210
01:26:30,423 --> 01:26:31,723
(Gosh, Mom)

2211
01:26:32,293 --> 01:26:33,823
(Is there ramyeon that ladies like?)

2212
01:26:34,723 --> 01:26:35,793
(You're the one who wants to eat it!)

2213
01:26:36,123 --> 01:26:37,133
(Don't get cute with me.)

2214
01:26:37,363 --> 01:26:38,462
Open wide, Mom.

2215
01:26:38,463 --> 01:26:41,163
(We're Like Family)

2216
01:26:42,163 --> 01:26:43,203
(I'm a fan of yours!)

2217
01:26:43,873 --> 01:26:46,102
(His popularity is increasing a great deal these days.)

2218
01:26:46,103 --> 01:26:47,303
(The appearance of a new market prince?)

2219
01:26:47,673 --> 01:26:48,942
(Hello, I've been living alone for 9 years.)

2220
01:26:48,943 --> 01:26:51,343
Hello, I'm Actor Seo Bum June.

2221
01:26:55,083 --> 01:26:56,913
(He's super gentle at home.)

2222
01:26:57,853 --> 01:26:59,652
(Today's a day off.)

2223
01:26:59,653 --> 01:27:01,783
(Having a half cheat day after a long time)

2224
01:27:02,423 --> 01:27:03,692
(It's a half cheat day because I don't eat...)

2225
01:27:03,693 --> 01:27:05,053
(that much.)

2226
01:27:05,893 --> 01:27:08,323
(Having a sandwich in the morning as soon as he wakes up)

2227
01:27:09,733 --> 01:27:12,233
(It was the perfect menu for a day off.)

2228
01:27:12,893 --> 01:27:15,403
(Bread is my life.)

2229
01:27:16,303 --> 01:27:17,773
(He starts his cheat day in earnest.)

2230
01:27:18,733 --> 01:27:20,443
(He's the rising star in the bread eating show scene.)

2231
01:27:21,073 --> 01:27:22,103
Sit.

2232
01:27:22,343 --> 01:27:24,273
(Stop eating.)

2233
01:27:25,173 --> 01:27:27,313
(Monde, shall we go for a walk?)

2234
01:27:28,183 --> 01:27:30,913
(Enjoying his holiday refreshingly)

2235
01:27:31,813 --> 01:27:33,553
(Shall we run excitedly?)

2236
01:27:33,983 --> 01:27:35,052
Let's go.

2237
01:27:35,053 --> 01:27:37,893
(What's wrong?)

2238
01:27:38,323 --> 01:27:39,493
Monde, hold on.

2239
01:27:39,823 --> 01:27:41,723
(I haven't had a day off in a while, but today isn't any easier.)

2240
01:27:42,593 --> 01:27:44,533
(He ends up running while walking his dog.)

2241
01:27:45,663 --> 01:27:49,033
(It May Not Be Perfect, But It's the Taste of a Day Off)
